1: 80
Paragraph 1
In theory, the solution based on constructing the arrangement of dual hyperplanes provides a logarithmic time for answering theDAR queries. It, however, is not practical especially when the number of ranking attributes is not small ( ≥3), since the size of the arrangement (hence, the space complexity) increases exponentially withd. Therefore, in this section, we propose practical solutions that keep the space complexity linear, i.e., O(n). Our algorithms are based on the computational geometric concept of ε-samples [ 27] (also introduced in Section 3).

